; Rotary radius check: o<ferrum_rotary_plausible> call [radius] [nominal
; radius] [where]. Aborts if the radius is not positive or differs from the
; nominal by more than max(0.25 x nominal, 2 mm). [where] names the touch
; in the message: 0 top at A start, 1 side at A+90, 2 side at A-90, 3 top
; at A+90, 4 top at A+180, 5 top at A+270. No motion.
o<ferrum_rotary_plausible> sub
#<tol> = [0.25 * #2]
o100 if [#<tol> LT [2 * #<_ferrum_mm>]]
    #<tol> = [2 * #<_ferrum_mm>]
o100 endif
o110 if [[#1 GT 0] AND [ABS[#1 - #2] LE #<tol>]]
    o<ferrum_rotary_plausible> return
o110 endif
o120 if [#3 EQ 0]
    (ABORT, Top radius at A start is not positive or too far from the diameter estimate; check WCS Y0 Z0 on the rotary axis)
o120 elseif [#3 EQ 1]
    (ABORT, A+90 side radius is too far from the diameter estimate)
o120 elseif [#3 EQ 2]
    (ABORT, A-90 side radius is too far from the diameter estimate)
o120 elseif [#3 EQ 3]
    (ABORT, A+90 top radius is too far from the diameter estimate)
o120 elseif [#3 EQ 4]
    (ABORT, A+180 top radius is too far from the diameter estimate)
o120 else
    (ABORT, A+270 top radius is too far from the diameter estimate)
o120 endif
o<ferrum_rotary_plausible> endsub
M2
